---
title: Custom scripts — compiled in-process, executed out of it
---
%% Verified against the tree on 2026-08-28. See docs/SANDBOX_DESIGN.md for the threat model.
%% The design rule, stated in RoslynScriptingService: the sandbox exists for ACCIDENTS in
%% trusted-user code, not for hostile tenants. The wall against hostile use is DemoPolicy,
%% which refuses to compile at all on any host that is not Full.
flowchart TD
    USER["User writes a custom indicator or strategy<br/>(Alt+, opens the custom scripts modal)"]
    GATE{"DemoPolicy.AllowCustomScripts<br/>Mode == Full?"}
    USER --> GATE
    GATE -->|no — Demo or Hosted| REFUSE["InvalidOperationException at the entry point.<br/>Compiling user code runs it server-side; that is desktop-only.<br/>Every compile and execute path funnels through this one check,<br/>so a future caller that skips the UI still hits the wall."]
    GATE -->|yes| WALK

    WALK["Semantic walker — the blocklist<br/>(reflection, process start, file and socket access, dynamic, …)"]
    WALK --> COMPILE["Roslyn compile against a DECLARED reference set,<br/>not a scan of AppDomain.CurrentDomain.GetAssemblies().<br/>Microsoft.CSharp is deliberately absent so the dynamic escape<br/>cannot reach the compiler. Identical on desktop, WebHost and test."]

    COMPILE --> HOST["OutOfProcessScriptHost<br/>LoadAssembly · Calculate · Evaluate over a pipe"]
    HOST --> PICK{"CreateDefaultLauncher —<br/>which sandbox does this OS have?"}

    PICK -->|Linux| BW["LinuxBwrapLauncher — bubblewrap<br/>read-only root, no network, private /tmp, own PID namespace"]
    PICK -->|Windows| AC["WindowsAppContainerLauncher — AppContainer SID,<br/>capability-less token"]
    PICK -->|macOS| SE["MacSandboxExecLauncher — sandbox-exec profile"]
    PICK -->|Android| AND["AndroidIsolatedProcessLauncher — isolatedProcess service"]
    PICK -->|iOS / Mac Catalyst| NOPE["ScriptingNotSupportedOnPlatformException at COMPILE time.<br/>No usable primitive, and refusing loudly beats<br/>silently falling back to in-process."]
    PICK -->|primitive missing at runtime| POLICY

    subgraph POLICY["SandboxPolicy — the fallback is not silent"]
        THROW["EnforceOrThrow: ScriptSandboxUnavailableException by default,<br/>carrying details AND a remedy"]
        OVR["ACCESSIBLETRADER_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED_SCRIPTS=1<br/>is the only way past it"]
        EVT["and taking it records a security event,<br/>so the override never happens invisibly"]
        THROW --> OVR --> EVT
    end

    BW & AC & SE & AND --> WORKER

    subgraph WORKER["AccessibleTrader.ScriptWorker — a separate OS process"]
        RUN["Runs the compiled IL"]
        OOP["OutOfProcessIndicator / OutOfProcessStrategy<br/>look like ordinary providers to the rest of the app"]
        RUN --> OOP
    end

    WORKER --> BACK["Results come back over the pipe.<br/>A crash, a hang or an OOM kills a child process, not the terminal."]

    TRAP["Learned the hard way: bwrap's --die-with-parent is PDEATHSIG on the spawning THREAD,<br/>so retiring a threadpool thread SIGKILLed live script workers mid-session.<br/>Three passes filed it as a test flake. The failure message said exit 137."]
    BW --- TRAP
